# Enforcing Capacity Allocation Frameworks

A practical guide for Scrum Masters, Delivery Leads, and Engineering Managers to maintain pipeline health, manage technical debt, and balance business delivery using capacity allocation models (such as the 70/20/10 rule).

---

## 1. What is Capacity Allocation?

**Capacity Allocation** is the practice of reserving pre-agreed percentages of a team’s sprint capacity (story points or total available hours) for specific types of work. 

Without explicit capacity limits, Product Owners naturally prioritize **100% business features** to hit aggressive delivery milestones. Over time, this leads to accumulated technical debt, fragile architecture, unoptimized data pipelines, and team burnout.

