Phase 1: Diagnosing the "Data Tech Debt Trap" (10 Mins)
[SAFe Coach]: "Thanks for jumping on, PO. Look at our last three sprints on Jira. We missed our PI Objectives by 25%, and in the last retrospective, the data engineers mentioned that 40% of their sprint was eaten up by unexpected pipeline outages, schema failures, and unoptimized dbt queries. Why do you think we keep hitting this wall?"

[Product Owner]: "Honestly, stakeholder pressure is huge right now. Marketing wants three new dashboards, and the business team needs new churn prediction ML endpoints. I know the engineers are struggling with legacy queries, but if I don't commit to these features, leadership thinks we aren't delivering value."

[SAFe Coach]: (Navigates to Frame 1 in Miro) "I hear you. But here is the reality in SAFe for Data Teams: Features built on top of failing pipelines are fake velocity. When we pack 100% of a sprint with business features, we aren't avoiding technical debt—we are just paying for it later with interest during production outages. Today, we're putting a framework in place that protects both your business targets and the team's pipeline health."

Phase 2: Introducing the 70/20/10 Allocation Model (20 Mins)
[SAFe Coach]: (Moves to Frame 2 in Miro showing the 70/20/10 Breakdown) "In SAFe, we treat capacity allocation as a financial portfolio. We don't negotiate individual refactoring tasks every sprint. Instead, we establish a non-negotiable capacity agreement between you, the System Architect, and the Data Team."

