# SAFe Capacity Allocation Policy: Data & Analytics Squads

## 1. Core Principle
To ensure pipeline stability, high data quality, and predictable throughput, all Data & Analytics squads adhere to a **70/20/10 Capacity Allocation Framework**. Capacity is calculated based on historical sprint velocity prior to Sprint Planning.

---

## 2. Allocation Categorization & Rules

| Category | Target % | Owner | Scope & Criteria |
| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |
| **Business Features** | **70%** | Product Owner | User-facing analytical value, new dashboards, ML endpoints, business report modifications. |
| **Technical Enablers** | **20%** | System Architect / Lead Engineer | Pipeline infrastructure upgrades, dbt/Airflow framework updates, IAM security automation, Data Contracts. |
| **Technical Debt & Bugs** | **10%** | Engineering Team | Query refactoring, test suite expansion, schema documentation, deprecation of obsolete assets. |

---

## 3. Governance & Enforcers

1. **Jira Field Requirement:** All Jira issues must have the `Work Category` field populated during Backlog Refinement.
2. **Sprint Planning Gate:** The Scrum Master / Delivery Lead will validate that candidate sprint backlogs do not exceed the $70\%$ Business Feature cap.
3. **Quarterly Review:** Capacity allocations are reviewed prior to each SAFe Program Increment (PI) Planning event to adapt to system maturity.
